sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/airspeed-scales-with-wing-loading-one-half-non-bird> a delphi:Hypothesis, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Across non-bird fliers, airspeed grows as the square root of wing loading: untested at this power" ;
    dct:description "Thompson's argument predicts that characteristic airspeed v scales with wing loading W/S to the power 1/2. On the taxa with a fetched W/S and speed, fitted separately for gliders and powered fliers as pre-registered: gliders n = 2 (flying fish, northern flying squirrel), too few for a fit; powered fliers n = 6 (three bats, three hoverflies), log-log slope 0.42 with 95 percent CI 0.11 to 0.73, but the wing loadings span 0.93 decades against the pre-registered minimum of 1.0. Both verdicts are inconclusive (underpowered). The pooled slope across all 8 points, 0.54 +- 0.09 (r2 0.85), is descriptive only because it mixes two physical regimes." ;
    rdfs:comment "Identifier note: the Bahlman et al. 2013 DOI cited in prov:wasDerivedFrom above is real. It resolved in Crossref on 2026-10-31T18:15:48Z with matching title and journal (physics/prior-art/raw/cr-bahlman-2013.json) and the full text was read from PubMed Central PMC3565731. The Delphi lint's fabricated-DOI pattern matches the Royal Society year.number article form and reports it as DUMMY-DOI; that is a false positive and the real identifier is kept." ;
    delphi:context "Claim under test: thompson1917-ch02-06 (D Arcy Thompson 1917, On Growth and Form, ch. II, Project Gutenberg 55264 lines 1716-1790), with thompson1917-ch02-07 and thompson1917-ch02-10. Taxon: Exocoetidae, NCBI Taxonomy 76072, GBIF 2968. Class Aves is the frozen holdout (holdout/exam.json); no bird value enters this record." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-thompson-ch02-06-reading-A> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1242/jeb.046052>, <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2012.0794>, <https://doi.org/10.1093/icb/icag077> ;
    skos:scopeNote "Assumed, not proved: constant air density and lift coefficient across taxa, which is what turns the lift equation into a slope of 1/2." ;
    rdfs:comment "Status: inconclusive. Does not establish: the truth or falsity of the scaling law; it records that the accessible data cannot decide it at the pre-registered power. The bat and hoverfly values come from a compilation whose primary sources were not fetched and whose mass and area columns disagree with its wing-loading column for insects by a factor of 5 to 8. Bat speeds are wind-tunnel test speeds, not cruising speeds. No bird enters the fit (Aves holdout). The next team needs three or more glider taxa with first-hand wing loading and speed (Davenport 1992 and Fish 1990 full texts would supply flying-fish species) before this reading can be decided." ;
    rdfs:comment "Pre-registration: physics/tests/thompson1917-ch02-06/result.json, written 2026-10-31T18:21:00Z before any wing loading, lifting area or lift coefficient was read, amended 2026-10-31T18:26:00Z before any fit ran (the file lists both and the values seen before each); sha256 at build 0094c084db22278a5f98d96cc2971ccd27813b0acdc458d60cadf7c7b7bcae48. The git commit that timestamps it is pending: the physics thread does not commit; the hub does." ;
    skos:related <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/thompson1917-ch02-06> ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/physics-thompson-ch02-06-reading-A> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Ordinary least squares of log10 airspeed on log10 wing loading, gliders and powered fliers separately" ;
    dct:description "Points: Cypselurus hiraii (W/S) with family-level field airspeed (glider): W/S 46.39 N/m2, v 15.00 m/s, W/S measured (Park and Choi 2010); airspeed second-hand field range 10-20 m/s; Glaucomys sabrinus (glider): W/S 59.00 N/m2, v 7.20 m/s, measured (speed); published population values (mass and wing loading) (bahlman-2013); Glossophaga soricina (powered): W/S 11.05 N/m2, v 4.30 m/s, secondary-compilation (span-efficiency-2026); Leptonycteris yerbabuenae (powered): W/S 14.25 N/m2, v 3.27 m/s, secondary-compilation (span-efficiency-2026); Plecotus auritus (powered): W/S 6.50 N/m2, v 3.00 m/s, secondary-compilation (span-efficiency-2026); Episyrphus balteatus (powered): W/S 1.97 N/m2, v 1.80 m/s, secondary-compilation (span-efficiency-2026); Eristalis pertinax (powered): W/S 2.73 N/m2, v 1.40 m/s, secondary-compilation (span-efficiency-2026); Syrphus ribesii (powered): W/S 1.67 N/m2, v 1.80 m/s, secondary-compilation (span-efficiency-2026). Gliders: n 2, decades 0.10, n = 2 < 5; W/S spans 0.10 decades < 1. Powered: n 6, slope 0.419, CI 0.112 to 0.727, r2 0.78, decades 0.93, W/S spans 0.93 decades < 1. Pooled descriptive slope 0.535 +- 0.092." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/hypothesis/airspeed-scales-with-wing-loading-one-half-non-bird> ;
    rdfs:comment "Computed by physics/analysis.py from physics/glide-data.csv (sha256 bc24245b5163723b192e95fccf714ef6e4b3b28e71df4fef3befbaf008a00635) and physics/comparison-data.csv (sha256 e0d3d74639c1fe856fe5128c1783151596fde3acc923a2409be3d3f870cc394a); numbers in physics/results.json (sha256 63336841c0d4c9ae2760ae5c87a9251b97218e3ebfdd453cad4cffb9cdf6ba0b). Every input value carries its source, locator, retrieval time and value kind in those files." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/results.json>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/glide-data.csv>, <https://delphi-mission-control.ashenoy000.workers.dev/t/physics/data/comparison-data.csv> .
}

